### F4 — lexical `expected_hit_at_10` is expected-Recall (WRONG number, HIGH)

- File: `top10_comparison_r1/data/run_lexical.py:55-76`. The function buckets equal scores, then for full buckets `exp += gb`, for the boundary bucket `exp += (10-better)*gb/len(idx)`, and returns `exp/len(gset)`. That is the expected-Recall@10 formula (identical in structure to `baseline/metrics_top10.py:104-131` `expected_recall_at_k`), NOT expected-Hit@10 (which needs `1 - C(B-gb,take)/C(B,take)` per `metrics_top10.py:134-168`; PQ's `run_pq.py:145-175` has the correct form).
- Stored effect: `data/per_query_bm25.jsonl` and `per_query_tfidf.jsonl` (705 rows each) carry the mislabeled column; `data/tdd_lexical.log` prints `bm25 ... expHit@10=0.4316` and `tfidf ... expHit@10=0.4191`.
- Command: averaged stored `expected_hit_at_10` vs `hit_at_10`/`recall_at_10` over both files.
- Observed: stored-exp mean == recall mean to <1e-9 on both arms (bm25 0.4316==0.4316 with hit 0.5418; tfidf 0.4191==0.4191 with hit 0.5291). Gold-size distribution from the same file: 319x1, 178x2, 92x3, ... (54.8% multi-gold), so the formulas genuinely differ — for single-gold queries they coincide, which likely masked the bug.
- Impact boundary: headline lexical Hit@10/Recall/nDCG recompute correctly in-test (F3 GREEN); no STOP-verdict input uses lexical expHit. True expected-Hit values are UNVERIFIED (need full lexical score vectors; only top-10 scores are stored).

