## (4) What I could NOT check and why

1. Full `audit_top10.py` end-to-end rerun (9440 structural + tie-order + 30-query cache rescore): bounded-time choice; I verified aggregates + structural-hit sample + 2-query rescore instead. The committed `audit_top10.log` claims 0/0/0 mismatches — consistent with but not independently re-proven by me. Needed: one ~5-15 min cache-rescore run (caches are present).
2. PQ retrain reproducibility (seed variance, faiss-version sensitivity): `run_pipeline()` writes into `pq/` (forbidden to execute in place) and takes ~112 s + faiss nondeterminism questions; rerunning elsewhere risks path/SHA drift. Single-seed variance therefore UNVERIFIED — needs a 2-3-seed retrain in a scratch dir.
3. True lexical expected-Hit@10 magnitudes: only top-10 scores are stored; full N-length score vectors are not persisted. Needs a `run_lexical.py` rescore or formula fix + rerun (data-owner scope).
4. PQ REPORT "4/705 cutoff ties": my 39/705 counts any adjacent equal pair in stored top-10, a weaker proxy. Needs full score vectors from codes+centroids (doable per query, not run corpus-wide).
5. LME cache cross-check beyond one sample row (`001be529`, N=514): 470 single-row ckpts union cleanly to 470 merged rows, but per-row N-vs-cache verified on sample only. Needs a 470-iteration cache loop.
6. Cost/timing rows (fit 0.38 s, scoring 25.06 s, rank 81.88 s, RSS): not remeasured; wall-clock claims are environment-specific and untestable read-only.
7. Other-dataset/width generality of round-2's inductive collapse: explicitly out of role (RealTalk k=96 only per brief).

